Title: Orion API - Build
Keywords: REST,API
Status: draft
Dependencies: *.md.en

{# lede #}This document covers the **Build System** APIs{# lede #}.

Basically, the build system is governed by two user-supplied Perl modules: [`lib/path.pm`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/path.pm) and [`lib/view.pm`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/view.pm).

The former's job is to do three things:

0. load [`lib/facts.yml`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/facts.yml) and [`lib/acl.yml`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/acl.yml),
1. construct [`@path::patterns`](#), and
2. opportunistically walk the [`content/`](#) tree to seed [`%path::dependencies`](#) and [`@path::acls`](#).

The latter's job is to provide invokable [`view`](#)-based methods for the matching entries in [`@path::patterns`](#), invoked as so...

```perl
#api
  ...

  my $path = "/content-rooted/path/to/source/file";

  for my $p (@path::patterns) {
    my ($re, $method, $args) = @$p;
    next unless $path =~ $re;
    ++$matched;

    my ($content, $mime_extension, $final_args, @new_sources) = view->can($method)->(path => $path, lang => $lang, %$args);

... write UTF $content to target file with associated $mime_extension file-type
  }

  copy_if_newer($path, "$ENV{TARGET}/content$path") unless $matched;

  ...
#api
```


